v2.0.0 (unreleased)
===================
-refactored the public API to use the aeon namespace and consistent lowercase
 underscore_style class and method names, while keeping the original object-oriented socket design
-updated the public C++ baseline to C++20, with optional C++23 implementation support
-retained IPv4/IPv6 address handling and hostname resolution from the later 1.20-devel work
-reworked TCP and UDP client/server implementations with explicit native socket ownership,
 retry-safe connection handling, and safer cleanup on failures
-preserved connect/read/write/accept timeout support and platform-specific error tracking
-fixed sized reads to respect caller buffer limits and preserve binary data, including embedded NULs
-preserved bounds-safe ReadLine behavior under the renamed read_line() interface
-centralized platform-specific socket handling and retained one-time Windows socket initialization
-retained the 60-second upper limit for accepted-connection timeouts
-added server-owned TCP, UDP and event peers with explicit removal and parent association
-changed accept() to return borrowed server-owned peers instead of transferring ownership to callers
-kept socket_set as a non-owning collection and restored broadcast support through virtual socket writes
-changed event_socket_set to non-owning registrations; applications must deregister sockets
 before destroying them or their owning server
-replaced legacy OnRead and per-socket Poll interfaces with application-driven
 event_socket_set polling, callbacks, and virtual event handlers
-restored direct-write send-result notifications through event_socket::on_write,
 while keeping on_drain separate for queued-output completion
-added TCP and UDP event clients and listeners with readiness, data, error and lifecycle callbacks
-added bounded, binary-safe queued TCP writes, configurable queue limits, partial-send handling,
 per-poll send budgets and drain notifications
-added transport-aware event I/O so encrypted event sockets cannot bypass TLS through raw send/recv
-added optional OpenSSL TLS clients with strict certificate trust and DNS/IP identity verification
-added explicit self-signed leaf certificate support without bypassing peer identity checking
-added TLS servers with server-owned encrypted peers, certificate/key validation and handshake timeouts
-added nonblocking TLS event clients and listeners using the existing event_socket_set callbacks
 and encrypted write queues
-fixed nonblocking TLS handshake readiness transitions and added configurable handshake deadlines,
 including cancellation and timeouts during indefinite poll waits
-fixed TLS session cleanup on cancelled connections and reconnect attempts
-fixed Windows TLS DLL exports by exporting individual member functions rather than STL-containing classes
-added separately selectable SSL and event socket support; plain TCP and UDP remain usable in SSL builds
-added shared and static library targets with public C++20 consumer checks and optional C++23 internals
-made tests, examples and benchmarks opt-in so ordinary builds produce only the libraries
-added regression tests for socket ownership, TCP/UDP event polling, write queues and real TLS
 handshakes in both shared and static library builds
-added chat, HTTP and UDP Pong examples, with supporting documentation and integration tests
-updated the Sphinx, Doxygen and Breathe documentation and expanded cross-platform build/test workflows
-retained ARM build support, branch-based version detection and explicit platform/compiler configuration
-removed the deprecated no-argument socket-set Add() overloads and old net::C* interface spellings

v1.19.2
=======
-fixed socket set error state initialization in constructors
-centralized platform-specific macros to libaeon.h
-corrected SetAcceptTimeout cap from 600s to 60s per audit
-removed outdated documentation.h file
-removed obsolete verbinclude reference from doxygen comments

v1.19.1
=======
-fixed off-by-one buffer overflow in ReadLine() CRLF detection with bounds-safe null-termination
-fixed memory leak in CEventSocketSet::Add() by replacing make_unique().release() with explicit new
-fixed missing timeout validation in SetAcceptTimeout() to prevent INT_MAX overflow
-added [[deprecated]] attribute to CSocketSet::Add() for compiler warnings
-added [[deprecated]] attribute to CEventSocketSet::Add() for compiler warnings
-added explicit destructor to CEventSocketSet to automatically cleanup sockets
-removed redundant SafeClearBuffer() call in ReadLine() loop for performance
-improved ownership semantics consistency between CSocketSet and CEventSocketSet

v1.19.0
=======
-fixed critical socket leak in CClientSocket::Connect() retry loop when trying multiple addresses
-fixed CSocket::Read(int size) ignoring size parameter, always reading MaxBufferSize-1 bytes
-added missing GET_NET_SOCKET_ERROR() macro definitions to CSocketUDP.cpp and CEventSocket.cpp for proper error handling
-removed redundant per-instance WSAStartup() call in CSocketUDP constructor (already handled globally)
-refactored CServerSocket::Accept() to return std::unique_ptr<CEventSocket> instead of raw pointers, eliminating memory leak risk
-added new SOCK_BIND error state constant for accurate error diagnostics when port binding fails
-implemented functional connect timeout support in CClientSocket::Connect() using non-blocking connect and select()
-refactored timeout helper functions WaitForReadable() and WaitForWritable() from file-scoped statics to CSocket protected static methods
-updated example code (hello-world.cpp, simple-server.cpp) to demonstrate modern C++11 memory management patterns
-added comprehensive documentation for Accept() API changes and connect timeout implementation

v1.18.2
=======
-fixed documentation
-removed outdated doxygen files
-fix builds to use target branch on merge

v1.18.1
=======
-fixed branch name extraction for build 

v1.18.0
=======
-added comprehensive Sphinx + Doxygen + Breathe documentation system with GitHub Pages deployment
-added automatic API reference generation from C++ code comments via Doxygen
-added GitHub Actions workflow for automatic documentation building and deployment to GitHub Pages
-added ARM cross-compilation support with optional -DARM_ARCH parameter (armv7-a, armv8-a, etc.)
-improved CMakeLists.txt platform and architecture detection logic
-implemented semantic versioning workflow with intelligent branch/tag detection
-all compiler warnings eliminated across all supported platforms (Linux GCC/Clang, Windows MSVC/MinGW, macOS, ARM)
-validated builds on 6 platform/compiler combinations without warnings or errors
-modernized code across all classes and platforms, updated c++ standard
-finalized move to github for all future releases

